Status: deployed and verified at https://elpis.masihmoafi.com on Vercel deployment `dpl_AjpgWs9EWUyHo7AsAD5S9W3f7AfJ`. All 11 focused site checks pass. Chromium verification covered 1440px and 390px layouts, provider changes, stable console and switcher dimensions, hover/focus marquee pausing, visible SVG motion, reduced-motion handling, and horizontal overflow. The public custom domain returned HTTP 200 with the corrected copy and no page or console errors.

## 2026-09-04 — ACE visual correction

Intent: replace the unrealistic static website mock with a scroll-driven Elpis terminal simulation grounded in the real chat composer, Context Ledger, and `/context` UI, while exploring a restrained Ratatui-achievable redesign before integrating it into the public site.

Acceptance:

- Preserve the recognizable Elpis chat, tool-call, composer, and Ledger structure.
- Show ACE intercepting tool output before model admission without changing the tool-call envelope.
- Let page scroll drive prompt entry, tool streaming, evidence compression, and model continuation.
- Use a restrained terminal palette and motion; no fake video controls, rainbow styling, or separate explanatory dashboard.
- Review the isolated visual prototype with Masih before replacing the website scene.

Status: implementation complete and locally verified, awaiting Masih's visual acceptance. The standalone site now uses daisyUI 5 with Tailwind CSS 4; the scroll sequence, populated Ledger, corrected `/context`, lifecycle SVG, desktop/mobile layout, and reduced-motion path are integrated. Website tests pass 9/9, Chromium reports no page/console errors or body overflow, and the portfolio production build validates 21 routes. Nothing was committed or deployed. Exact evidence and remaining acceptance are recorded in `SESSION_HANDOFF.md`.

