## 2026-09-05 — Website context and rectangle spacing

Follow-up intent: repair the reported terminal/Ledger clipping, without changing copy, colors, or the scroll sequence. Acceptance: frame and both panes fit at 987px and 1280px with no horizontal overflow; commands, raw output and Ledger rows wrap inside their pane; mobile stacks panes; forward/reverse scrolling preserves the existing animation. The published 1160px fixed-width layout fails this check (922px available). Work is scoped to website CSS and its regression check, not the Rust application.

Follow-up evidence: the new regression test failed against the old fixed-width CSS, then all 10 website checks and the CSS build passed. In-app inspection measured zero horizontal overflow in frame, terminal, chat, Ledger, output, composer and footer at 987px, 1280px and 390px. At 987px, forward scrolling moved tools to ACE and reverse returned to tools at the same scroll position. The live domain serves stylesheet v7 and byte-identical reviewed HTML/CSS on deployment dpl_3LD4gomYsFp8eYcBoKwqhryJXMmD (website-nd8vmapey-masihmoafis-projects.vercel.app). Live 987px inspection confirms wrapped output and zero horizontal overflow. Vertical pane scrolling is retained. No Rust, copy, color, candidate, or GitHub changes. Masih's acceptance remains open. The preceding deployment website-81j4dp2fd-masihmoafis-projects.vercel.app remains available for rollback by restoring the custom-domain alias.

Intent: make the website context visual visible without a reveal trigger, add the requested chart views, and give all text-bearing rectangles breathing room.

Acceptance: inspect all ten SVG labels for at least 24px horizontal clearance; check cards, context panels, terminal panels, and installation command padding in the in-app browser; retain readable diagram labels at narrow widths; build and run the focused website checks. No Rust or deployment changes.

Status: local build and website test suite pass; git diff --check is clean. In-app browser inspection covered the default desktop viewport, the reported 950px width, and 390px mobile. All ten SVG boxes have at least 24px horizontal text clearance at intrinsic scale; notes have at least 16px vertical clearance. Cards have 24-32px padding; mobile stats stack; the install command wraps within its panel and Copy retains its label, font size, and dimensions. The terminal frame ends inside the viewport, and scrolling forward/back returns to the same phase and position. Diagram URL versioning prevents the old cached boxes from persisting. No deployment or Rust changes. Masih's visual acceptance remains open.
